From: Ravikant Cherukuri <ravi@openloopagentics.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 01:58:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add a commits widget: three counts in one button

Nothing on the strip said how much work had actually landed, and the answer
lives on another machine entirely -- the repos are on the Mac mini, not here.

Add a `commits` widget reading today / this week / this month from a TOML
file, drawn as three whole numbers under one-letter tags. Counts, not
proportions, so there are no bars: at arm's length the figure itself is the
thing worth reading. Recency carries the emphasis, today at full strength and
the longer windows set back, so the eye lands on the number that moves.

File-backed like the usage bars, and for the same reason -- the daemon runs
as `nobody` after privdrop and cannot read a home directory. It dims the
whole button when the file stops being refreshed, because a counter that
cannot say it is stale quietly lies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UmcdUC47KEJPE7hWccLyV6
